[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Quests/ObjectiveResource.cs" id="2_obj"]

; The Veiled Archive's admission trial (Phase 42G). "A person joins us by bringing us something we
; did not have" is Keeper Ysolde Marr's own line from her 42B stranger greeting — the whole brief for
; this quest is that line, made playable. Tam Quillfellow's Scriptorium (38L) already sells a copy of
; the Treatise on Wardings "the Veiled Archive would rather nobody had copied" (his shop file's own
; comment); this quest is the seam that finally uses it. No new item, no new prop, no new cell.
;
; ⚠️ BOTH OBJECTIVES TARGET dialogue.tam THEN dialogue.archive_keeper, AND THE SECOND ONE NEEDS
; SEQUENTIAL. Talk objectives complete on ANY end of their dialogue, and this quest is OFFERED by the
; Keeper herself (her stranger branch) — so without ordering, ending the very conversation that starts
; the quest would also satisfy the report half in the same breath. SequentialObjectives is the safe
; answer here precisely because neither objective is Kill (42E's own trap): Talk repeats forever, so
; requiring obj_ask before obj_report live can never soft-lock, only ever ask the player to go first.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Obj_ask_tam"]
